Z||000000||NSUMEY||04-19-2001||11:42 PM||||84 2.5 My car was running fine until it got too hot and cracked the head. So I got a reman head new headbolts and pushrods, put the darn thing together and now it won't idle. It blows black smoke and the plugs are sooted up......any ideas? like I said it ran before....||||reg||9
Z||000001||84Bill||04-19-2001||11:49 PM||||Replace the O2 sensor. They don't like getting antifreeze on them, has a tendency to screw them up bigtime. also check you vaccume lines again just to be sure||||reg||1
Z||000002||thomas_l||04-20-2001||11:38 AM||||Check for any loose engine grounds. I left one off when I put my trans in and had a rough idle and rich (black smoke) exhaust. Hooked it up and everythings happy again.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||04-20-2001||01:16 PM||||Did you remember to hook up your MAP sensor when you put Humpty back together again?<P>(I've forgotten not once, but twice - got black smoke and a rough idle both times...)||||reg||5
Z||000004||88formula||04-20-2001||01:19 PM||||Do what Chadman said and check your map sensor.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||NSUMEY||04-20-2001||02:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by NSUMEY:<BR><B>84 2.5 My car was running fine until it got too hot and cracked the head. So I got a reman head new headbolts and pushrods, put the darn thing together and now it won't idle. It blows black smoke and the plugs are sooted up......any ideas? like I said it ran before....</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I checked for vacuum leaks...none<BR>map sensor is hooked up<BR>ground wires are all fine<BR>I thought the ecm didn't reference the o2 sensor until vehicle reached operating temp?<P>well....now the freakin' starter blew...think<BR>I'll be getting rid of this %$!#@% thing!!!!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||thomas_l||04-20-2001||03:42 PM||||Take a deep breath, scream at your neighbors, have a beer, and throw a few tools around just don't break anything. Then pretend like you are just getting started and work the simple things first. Your patience will pay off. If you know a second set of eyes, give them a beer too and let em have a look. You're probably gonna kick yourself when you finally figure out whatever the problem is. That's how it works for me anyway  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000007||NSUMEY||04-21-2001||10:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by NSUMEY:<BR><B> [QUOTE]Originally posted by NSUMEY:<BR>[b]84 2.5 My car was running fine until it got too hot and cracked the head. So I got a reman head new headbolts and pushrods, put the darn thing together and now it won't idle. It blows black smoke and the plugs are sooted up......any ideas? like I said it ran before....</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I checked for vacuum leaks...none<BR>map sensor is hooked up<BR>ground wires are all fine<BR>I thought the ecm didn't reference the o2 sensor until vehicle reached operating temp?<P>well....now the freakin' starter blew...think<BR>I'll be getting rid of this %$!#@% thing!!!![/B][/QUOTE]<P>well...replaced the ignition wires today....got it running and one of the rocker arms broke.....decided to do compression test....#1-25 #2-75 #3-110 #5-75 ...had the lifters backed all the way so both valves were closed......why the big difference????I tore the freakin head off again...starting off from scratch tomorrow......I JUST DON'T UNDERSTAND WHAT CAN BE THE PROBLEM....I NEVER MESSED WITH THE TIMING....THE VALVES ARE NON-ADJUSTABLE.....NO PROBLEM WITH THE PISONS OR THE RINGS BECAUSE THE BORES HOLD WATER...OH WELL .....TOMORROWS ANOTHER DAY||||reg||13
Z||000008||Seanh||04-21-2001||10:26 PM||||I think this sounds like a Lifter/valve train problem. Probally didn't need to remove the head again. (Trust me, I put new head gaskets in, started putting the engine back together, while putting the upper intake on I dropped a bolt down the intake and it went into the chamber, fun! (v6 by the way)) I am not to sure about the 4 cyl engine because Iv never worked with it much. Did you follow the porper procedure for valve lashing? Perhaps you may have over tightened your rocker arm bolts? Check it out before you do somthing you'll regret like selling the car (trust me on that one too, I wanted to so many times while doing to new engine but Im sooooo glad I didn't give up now)||||reg||1
Z||000009||NSUMEY||04-22-2001||02:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by NSUMEY:<BR><B> well...replaced the ignition wires today....got it running and one of the rocker arms broke.....decided to do compression test....#1-25 #2-75 #3-110 #5-75 ...had the lifters backed all the way so both valves were closed......why the big difference????I tore the freakin head off again...starting off from scratch tomorrow......I JUST DON'T UNDERSTAND WHAT CAN BE THE PROBLEM....I NEVER MESSED WITH THE TIMING....THE VALVES ARE NON-ADJUSTABLE.....NO PROBLEM WITH THE PISONS OR THE RINGS BECAUSE THE BORES HOLD WATER...OH WELL .....TOMORROWS ANOTHER DAY</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, back at it again......cleaned up the mating surfaces...had a buddy put a magnet thing??? to check for block cracks and found none...so back together again....I stopped in Advanced Auto to pick up the rocker arm kit that I called for yesterday and it all went down hill from there....the salesperson I spoke with yesterday said the kit came with the rocker arm, pivot and bolt.....got ready to install the rockers and find out I got no freakin bolt....I can't believe that a 99 cent bolt is keeping me down for another day...go figure!!! well have to wait until tomorrow after work to finish up....||||reg||9
Z||000010||NSUMEY||04-24-2001||09:28 AM||||well...still waiting on the rocker arm ball bolt....I can't believe those are so hard to get a hold of......the L4 was used in so many different applications you would think they would be everwhere....the fiero store doesn't even carry it???? cost--$4 freakin' bucks for 1||||reg||1
